SKIP

The class `FlowableBlockingSubscribe` only provides static helper methods that delegate to reactive‑stream components (`Publisher`, `Subscriber`, `BlockingSubscriber`, etc.). Its performance is tightly coupled to the behavior of the supplied `Publisher` implementation and the underlying concurrency primitives, not to any intrinsic algorithmic work that can be meaningfully isolated in a microbenchmark. Creating a JMH benchmark would require a concrete `Publisher` (e.g., a `Flowable`), turning the benchmark into a test of that publisher rather than the utility itself. Consequently, a dedicated JMH benchmark for this class is not warranted.